+#### [markdown]
+### A simplifying assumption: equal emissivities in both layers
+We have introduced **two new parameters**, the emissivities (or absorptivities, same thing) $\epsilon_0, \epsilon_1$. So our equations so far are general enough to account for very different atmospheric compositions (e.g., different absorbing gases or cloud amounts) in the two layers.
+To keep things simple, from here on **we are going to assume that both atmospheric layers have the same emissivity**, that is we assume
+$$ \epsilon_0 = \epsilon_1 = \epsilon $$
+With this assumption, the expression for the OLR reduces to
+$$\text{OLR} = (1-\epsilon)^2 \sigma T_s^4 + \epsilon(1-\epsilon)\sigma T_0^4 + \epsilon \sigma T_1^4$$
+This is the expression we will use to tune our model to observations in the next section.
